;; The classes of the Java forms' corpora the per-form differential check (bin/diffcheck;
;; doc/FUTAMURA-SURVEY.md, "F2 as built") does not give j2g, with the reasons: they stay
;; interpreted in both runs of the Java forms' pair. Binary names.
{:excluded
 [{:class "dcf.defclass.Clj"
   :reason "Clojure in a class body naming the namespace's vars (twice, *dyn*, defined by earlier Clojure cases): j2g analyzes the Java forms without the namespace's vars (Unable to resolve symbol: twice); the interpreter hands the body to the evaluator in the running namespace"}
  {:class "native.nested_deftype.Host"
   :reason "A deftype inside a class body (Clojure in the body, its class made at run time by the evaluator in the running namespace): j2g cannot name it (Unable to resolve class: user.InHost)"}
  {:class "cfcorpus.c50.A2"
   :reason "j2g fails on it (j2g: no Go type for nil, model.ae's go-type, in A2$1): an anonymous subclass of the member class In, with a constructor argument, whose method reads the outer instance's field f. The interpreter defines it. A j2g bug, found by this check (F2.2)"}
  {:class "cfcorpus.c3.Reduced"
   :reason "Implements clojure.lang.IDeref, a name the renamed runtime does not have (the corpus keeps the Java forms compiler's tests as they were): j2g's header fails (Unknown type) and the class it translates anyway declares getClass twice (an error), where the interpreter fails to define it"}
  {:class "cfcorpus.c6.Cov"
   :reason "Its reify implements CovBase and CovNarrow, interfaces of another test file of the corpus's origin that the corpus does not define: j2g's analysis fails (Unknown type) and the reify it translates anyway declares getClass twice (an error), where the interpreter fails to define it"}
  {:classes ["cfcorpus.c2.Sub" "cfcorpus.c4.Clj" "cfcorpus.c5.WithTypes" "cfcorpus.c8.OversTied" "cfcorpus.c43.Outer"]
   :reason "defclass_corpus.ae keeps each Java forms vector of the Java forms compiler's tests apart from the rest of its test file: these name classes or imports of that file the corpus does not have (classes.access_base.Base, CovNarrow, Iterator unimported), so j2g's analysis fails and the class, alone in its Go package, would leave the package empty (the build fails); the interpreter fails to define them too"}
  {:classes ["cfcorpus.c11.ClojureData" "cfcorpus.c16.F2"]
   :reason "Clojure in a class body naming the namespace's vars or a deftype made in the body at run time (twice, user.InBody): as dcf.defclass.Clj and native.nested_deftype.Host"}
  {:classes ["cfcorpus.c7.Overs" "cfcorpus.c13.NoRefl" "cfcorpus.c38.PkgB" "cfcorpus.c56.PO"]
   :reason "Classes the Java forms compiler's tests expect not to compile (an ambiguous overload, a member reached without reflection, a package-private member of another package, a value of a void method): j2g's analysis rejects them as the interpreter's does"}
  {:class "cfcorpus.c42.Methods"
   :reason "Declares a native method (Nat): a class of the program needs its Go implementation (j2g's natives, J2G-SPEC), which a test class has none of (undefined: Methods_Nat_I__J_native); the interpreter defines it, a call failing"}
  {:class "cfcorpus.c54.K"
   :reason "j2g drops the arguments of an anonymous class's super constructor chosen by :param-tags, (anon K ^{:param-tags [int]} [9]): K$1's constructor calls K's Ctor_I without the int (Go: not enough arguments in call to t.K.Ctor_I), so the program does not build. The interpreter defines it. A j2g bug, found by this check (F2.2)"}
  {:class "cfcorpus.c57.PB"
   :reason "j2g passes the arguments of an anonymous subclass of the inner class In made with :outer, (anon In [k] :outer o ...), to the wrong constructors (Go: too many arguments in call to PB_1_New_PB, not enough in call to PB_In's Ctor_PB_I), so the program does not build. The interpreter defines it. A j2g bug, found by this check (F2.2), with cfcorpus.c50.A2's and cfcorpus.c54.K's: anonymous classes with constructor arguments"}]}
